  "response_complete": true,
  "response_text": "Burnout from overtime and unrealistic deadlines can be a serious issue that can affect your physical and mental health. Here are some warning signs to watch for and practical recommendations to help prevent burnout:\n\nWarning signs:\n\n1. Physical symptoms: Fatigue, muscle tension, headaches, digestive problems, and changes in appetite.\n\n2. Emotional symptoms: Anxiety, irritability, depression, and a lack of motivation.\n\n3. Cognitive symptoms: Difficulty concentrating, memory problems, and a decrease in productivity.\n\n4. Behavioral symptoms: Neglecting personal and professional responsibilities, substance abuse, and a decline in social relationships.\n\nPractical recommendations:\n\n1. Set realistic goals: Break down your workload into manageable tasks and set realistic deadlines.\n\n2. Take breaks: Take regular breaks to rest and recharge, and avoid working too long without a break.\n\n3. Prioritize self-care: Make time for activities that you enjoy and that help you relax, such as exercise, meditation, or hobbies.\n\n4. Seek support: Talk to your supervisor or a trusted colleague about your workload and seek support from a mental health professional if needed.\n\n5. Practice self-compassion: Be kind to yourself and recognize that it's okay to ask for help when you need it.\n\nRemember, burnout is a serious issue that can have long-term consequences on your physical and mental health. Taking steps to prevent it is important to maintain your well-being and productivity.",
